    "caption": "What the Record Remembers, original instrumental closing credits miniature in D. One complete piece, a beginning, a second thought and a clearly authored last chord. Warm synth strings, sparse soft FM bell and felt mallet voices. A single rising fourth D G followed by F-sharp E D; the middle borrows a gentle G minor color, then returns. Leave the last four bars for a slowly spaced, reflective cadence, ending on a still open D fifth; instruments stop and their natural reverb falls away completely. Respectful, neither victorious nor tragic. No percussion flourish, no vocals, no repeat.",
